### From Heat in Place to Recoverable Heat

**SEC HIIP Claim:** The filing applies no heat recovery factor. It states that
*"a heat recovery factor assessment is still required to evaluate recoverable heat"*, and converts
thermal energy to electricity by applying a static 19.5% ORC plant efficiency and a 1.069 peak output
correction factor to the raw HIIP over 30 years, yielding a Mean Estimate Electric Power Capacity of
14,005 MW. That figure therefore describes the conversion of the entire in-place accumulation, not an
estimate of what can be produced from it.

**HIP-RA-X Evaluation:** That assessment is what HIP-RA-X performs. Running the same reservoir at the
228°C volume-weighted mean with the tool's recovery factors applied, rather than overridden to 1.0 as
in the baseline above, gives the following chain (10<sup>15</sup> Joules):

| Quantity | Result | Basis |
| :--- | ---: | :--- |
| Gross HIIP (D&M, Mean Estimate) | 63,560 | Total thermal energy in place |
| Stored Heat, recovery applied | {{ rec_stored_heat_15j }} | 75% recoverable heat from rock |
| Available Heat | {{ rec_available_heat_15j }} | Second-law limit on the recovered heat |
| Producible Heat | {{ rec_producible_heat_15j }} | Over the 30-year reservoir life cycle |

The resulting Recovery Factor of {{ rec_recovery_factor }}% — the proportion of heat in place that
reaches the surface as useful energy — is the quantity the filing identifies as missing.

Carried through to generation:

* **SEC HIIP Estimated Power Capacity (Mean):** 14,005 MW
* **HIP-RA-X Producible Electricity, un-risked (MC Mean):** {{ mc_elec_mean_mw }} MW
* **HIP-RA-X Producible Electricity, recovery applied:** {{ rec_elec_mw }} MW

The filing's figure is {{ dm_elec_ratio }} times the HIP-RA-X estimate. This is not a disagreement
about the resource: both describe the same rock at the same temperature, and the Gross HIIP estimates
agree to within 1%. It is the difference between the energy present and the energy obtainable, which
is the step the filing explicitly declines to take.

